\ Words the interpreter only has when it is a task rather than a machine.
\
\ Metacompiled after ansi-forth.fs, the same way an application's .fi file is,
\ so sym.awk has to see this file too or the symbols will not resolve.

only forth definitions
also meta-compiler
meta-compile

\ There is nowhere to go from a Forth that owns the whole device, so the
\ standard word is listed as unimplemented there.  Here there is a shell to
\ go back to.

code bye                  :: bye                     ( -- )
        xcall   Forth_exit
        NEXT
end-code

\ Left empty so cold falls through to forth.ini, as the interactive image
\ does; an application image stores its entry point here instead.

variable 'cold-run :: tick-cold-run
